{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":33,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.symmetric_point_exists_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.symmetric_point_exists_unique","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L289-L296","doc":"**The symmetric point exists and is unique.**  Combining the two: L6a4's\nfixed locus is exactly one point, the regular ideal octahedron — bean\n`qou-krvm` hypothesis (ii), TRUE for this anchor and FALSE for m004. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.Fixed_regularOctahedron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.Fixed_regularOctahedron","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L283-L287","doc":"It is fixed by the whole symmetry group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA_regularOctahedron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA_regularOctahedron","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L279-L281","doc":"It is feasible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.regularOctahedron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.regularOctahedron","kind":"def","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L273-L277","doc":"The regular ideal octahedron point: `1/2` on the size-8 orbit, `1/4`\nelsewhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.unique_symmetric_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.unique_symmetric_point","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L254-L265","doc":"**The unique symmetric point (bean qou-krvm hypothesis (ii), TRUE here).**\nA feasible point fixed by the symmetry group is exactly the regular ideal\noctahedron: `1/4` on the size-16 orbit, `1/2` on the size-8 orbit.\n\nContrast `M004AngleStructure.fixed_iff_line`, where the same hypothesis is\nFALSE and the fixed locus is one-dimensional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.fixed_orbitB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.fixed_orbitB","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L234-L252","doc":"A fixed point is **constant on the size-8 orbit** (representative `2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.fixed_orbitA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.fixed_orbitA","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L198-L232","doc":"A fixed point is **constant on the size-16 orbit** (representative `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.gen2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.gen2","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L192-L196","doc":"**Generator 2 preserves the angle structure.**  It permutes the\nconstraint rows among themselves; the proof is the resulting linear identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.gen1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.gen1","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L186-L190","doc":"**Generator 1 preserves the angle structure.**  It permutes the\nconstraint rows among themselves; the proof is the resulting linear identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.gen0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.gen0","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L180-L184","doc":"**Generator 0 preserves the angle structure.**  It permutes the\nconstraint rows among themselves; the proof is the resulting linear identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.Fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.Fixed","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L175-L178","doc":"A point is **fixed** when all three generators leave it unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.sigma2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.sigma2","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L147-L173","doc":"Symmetry generator 2 of the order-16 coordinate group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.sigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.sigma1","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L119-L145","doc":"Symmetry generator 1 of the order-16 coordinate group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.sigma0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.sigma0","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L91-L117","doc":"Symmetry generator 0 of the order-16 coordinate group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge7","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge6","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge5","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L87-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge4","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L86-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge3","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge2","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge1","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.edge0","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet7","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet6","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet5","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet4","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet3","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet2","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet1","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.tet0","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA.mk","kind":"ctor","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.GA","kind":"structure","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L71-L89","doc":"**The L6a4 generalised angle structure.**  SnapPy's 8 per-tetrahedron\nsums and 8 edge equations, in pi-units. Generated from the measured system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.Pt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.L6a4AngleStructure.Pt","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/L6a4AngleStructure.lean#L65-L69","doc":"The 24 tetrahedron angles of the L6a4 (Borromean rings) triangulation,\nin pi-units: 8 ideal tetrahedra, 3 angles each.  Indexed by `Nat` rather than\n`Fin 24` so the permutation generators reduce definitionally at literal indices;\ncoordinates past 23 are simply unconstrained and never referenced. ","signatureChunk":0}]}